# Reproducible from the ledger and the governed files; never the source of anything.
#
# THE LEDGER ITSELF IS COMMITTED. It is this graph's source of truth (Squiddy's one invariant: a
# projection is disposable, the events are not), and `seldon governed sync` reads it. Everything
# below is rebuilt from it by replay.
corpus/parsed/
corpus/resolved/
corpus/acquisition_state.json
work/
evidence/

# Pre-write snapshots. Squiddy copies the ledger before every append (DI-014), so a backfill over
# a hundred documents leaves a hundred copies of an ever-growing file. They are a crash-recovery
# convenience for the run in progress, not history: history is the ledger, and git holds that.
ledger/*.bak-*

# The KGX export and its node/edge sidecars: sixteen megabytes of JSON per release, every byte of
# it a replay of the ledger. `squiddy release --graph governed` regenerates them. EXPORT_VERSIONS.md
# and the release diff are NOT ignored — those are the small, pinned record OF a release (DI-110),
# and a release whose row is missing did not happen as far as the graph is concerned.
exports/*.json
exports/*.jsonl

# THE LEDGER IS RE-INCLUDED BY NAME (SEL-001). A host repository may ignore `*.jsonl` at its root
# (Arnold does); without this line the graph's source of truth would be silently left out of git.
!ledger/events.jsonl
